                <head>UR–18. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On October 10, 1960, the International Monetary Fund announced that an initial
                    par value for the Uruguayan peso had been established at 7.40 pesos per United
                    States dollar, by agreement between the Fund and the Government of Uruguay. The
                    fund also announced that it had entered into a stand-by agreement enabling the
                    Uruguayan Government to draw the equivalent of United States $30,000,000 over a
                    12-month period. Documentation concerning IMF activities in Uruguay is contained
                    in decimal file 833.10 and in ARA Files, Lot 62 D 359, “IMF.”</p>
            </div>
